content.text:
### Trust prompt explains what trust enables

Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/tui/src/onboarding/trust_directory.rs

The trust prompt shown on first run, explaining that trusting the directory allows project-local config, hooks, and exec policies to load.

```rust
"Do you trust the contents of this directory? Working with untrusted \
 contents comes with higher risk of prompt injection. Trusting the \
 directory allows project-local config, hooks, and exec policies to load."
```

--------------------------------

### ProjectConfig struct - Project-specific configuration options

Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/config/src/config_toml.rs

Shows that ProjectConfig only supports 'trust_level' field. Projects cannot override approval_policy, approvals_reviewer, or sandbox_mode. These are global config settings that apply to all directories regardless of project configuration.

```rust
#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, JsonSchema)]
#[schemars(deny_unknown_fields)]
pub struct ProjectConfig {
    pub trust_level: Option<TrustLevel>,
}

impl ProjectConfig {
    pub fn is_trusted(&self) -> bool {
        matches!(self.trust_level, Some(TrustLevel::Trusted))
    }

    pub fn is_untrusted(&self) -> bool {
        matches!(self.trust_level, Some(TrustLevel::Untrusted))
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Exact config.toml structure for a trusted project

Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/core/src/config/mod.rs

Comment in set_project_trust_level_inner showing the exact TOML syntax the current Codex CLI writes to mark a project path trusted/untrusted: a [projects] table with a quoted project path key and a trust_level entry.

```rust
    // Ensure we render a human-friendly structure:
    //
    // [projects]
    // [projects."/path/to/project"]
    // trust_level = "trusted" or "untrusted"
    //
    // rather than inline tables like:
    //
    // [projects]
    // "/path/to/project" = { trust_level = "trusted" }
```

### Codex network approvals / sandbox notes > How do I reduce repeated approval prompts?

Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/skills/src/assets/samples/imagegen/references/codex-network.md

If you trust the repo and want fewer prompts, use a configuration or profile that both: - enables network for the sandbox mode you plan to use - sets an approval policy that matches your risk tolerance If you want quieter automation after network is enabled, you can choose a stricter approval policy, but do that intentionally and with care.

--------------------------------

### FAQ > How do I choose sandbox access?

Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/sdk/python/docs/faq.md

Sandbox access is managed via presets: read_only, workspace_write, and full_access. Workspace_write is the default for projects with a recorded trust decision, allowing file operations within the workspace and configured roots. A sandbox override applied to a specific turn will also apply to subsequent turns.

