### Configure Ollama Local Provider

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/crush/blob/main/README.md

This configuration enables Crush to connect to a local Ollama server. Crush will auto-discover models from this provider if the models list is empty.

```json
{
  "providers": {
    "ollama": {
      "name": "Ollama",
      "base_url": "http://localhost:11434/v1/",
      "type": "ollama"
    }
  }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Custom API Provider

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/crush/blob/main/internal/skills/builtin/crush-config/SKILL.md

Add a custom provider by specifying its type, base URL, API key, and model details. The 'type' field is mandatory and can be one of several predefined values or a local provider type.

```json
{
  "providers": {
    "deepseek": {
      "type": "openai-compat",
      "base_url": "https://api.deepseek.com/v1",
      "api_key": "$DEEPSEEK_API_KEY",
      "models": [
        {
          "id": "deepseek-chat",
          "name": "Deepseek V3",
          "context_window": 64000
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### Custom Providers > Local Models

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/crush/blob/main/README.md

Crush can auto-discover local models from providers like llamacpp, omlx, lmstudio, litellm, or ollama by setting the provider type and leaving the models list empty. The provider name and base URL are typically required.

--------------------------------

### Custom Providers > OpenAI-Compatible APIs

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/crush/blob/main/README.md

To configure an OpenAI-compatible provider like Deepseek, specify the 'openai-compat' type, the base URL, and the API key. Models can be defined with their IDs, names, costs, context windows, and default max tokens.

--------------------------------

### Crush Config > Custom Providers

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/crush/blob/main/internal/skills/builtin/crush-config/SKILL.md

Custom providers can be configured with various types, including `openai`, `openai-compat`, `anthropic`, or local types like `llamacpp`. Essential configuration includes `type`, `base_url`, `api_key`, and `models`. Certain fields like `api_key` and `base_url` are subject to shell expansion.

