### Define Model struct in Go

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/catwalk/blob/main/_autodocs/types.md

The Model struct definition used to represent AI model metadata and pricing configurations.

```go
type Model struct {
    ID                     string       `json:"id"`
    Name                   string       `json:"name"`
    CostPer1MIn            float64      `json:"cost_per_1m_in"`
    CostPer1MOut           float64      `json:"cost_per_1m_out"`
    CostPer1MInCached      float64      `json:"cost_per_1m_in_cached"`
    CostPer1MOutCached     float64      `json:"cost_per_1m_out_cached"`
    ContextWindow          int64        `json:"context_window"`
    DefaultMaxTokens       int64        `json:"default_max_tokens"`
    CanReason              bool         `json:"can_reason"`
    ReasoningLevels        []string     `json:"reasoning_levels,omitempty"`
    DefaultReasoningEffort string       `json:"default_reasoning_effort,omitempty"`
    SupportsImages         bool         `json:"supports_attachments"`
    Options                ModelOptions `json:"options,omitzero"`
}
```

--------------------------------

### Provider JSON Schema

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/catwalk/blob/main/_autodocs/endpoints.md

Defines the structure of the provider and model configuration objects returned by the API.

```typescript
[
  {
    "name": string,
    "id": string,
    "api_key": string,  // optional, template string like "$ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"
    "api_endpoint": string,  // optional, template string
    "type": "openai" | "openai-compat" | "openrouter" | "vercel" | "anthropic" | "google" | "azure" | "bedrock" | "google-vertex",
    "default_large_model_id": string,  // optional
    "default_small_model_id": string,  // optional
    "models": [
      {
        "id": string,
        "name": string,
        "cost_per_1m_in": number,
        "cost_per_1m_out": number,
        "cost_per_1m_in_cached": number,  // optional
        "cost_per_1m_out_cached": number,  // optional
        "context_window": number,
        "default_max_tokens": number,
        "can_reason": boolean,
        "reasoning_levels": string[],  // optional
        "default_reasoning_effort": string,  // optional
        "supports_attachments": boolean,
        "options": {
          "temperature": number,  // optional
          "top_p": number,  // optional
          "top_k": number,  // optional
          "frequency_penalty": number,  // optional
          "presence_penalty": number,  // optional
          "provider_options": object  // optional
        }
      }
    ],
    "default_headers": object  // optional
  }
]
```

--------------------------------

### Define Provider struct in Go

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/catwalk/blob/main/_autodocs/types.md

The Provider struct represents the complete configuration for an AI provider, including credentials and model lists.

```go
type Provider struct {
    Name                string            `json:"name"`
    ID                  InferenceProvider `json:"id"`
    APIKey              string            `json:"api_key,omitempty"`
    APIEndpoint         string            `json:"api_endpoint,omitempty"`
    Type                Type              `json:"type,omitempty"`
    DefaultLargeModelID string            `json:"default_large_model_id,omitempty"`
    DefaultSmallModelID string            `json:"default_small_model_id,omitempty"`
    Models              []Model           `json:"models,omitempty"`
    DefaultHeaders      map[string]string `json:"default_headers,omitempty"`
}
```

--------------------------------

### Query OpenAI providers

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/catwalk/blob/main/_autodocs/providers-list.md

Identify OpenAI or OpenAI-compatible providers using the catwalk package constants.

```go
// OpenAI itself
provider := catwalk.InferenceProviderOpenAI

// OpenAI-compatible (Zhipu, Alibaba, etc.)
// Filter by type: TypeOpenAICompat
```

--------------------------------

### Filter Providers and Models in Go

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/catwalk/blob/main/_autodocs/usage-patterns.md

Filter providers by type or search for models with specific capabilities like extended reasoning.

```go
package main

import (
    "log"
    "charm.land/catwalk/pkg/embedded"
    "charm.land/catwalk/pkg/catwalk"
)

// FindProvidersByType returns all providers of a specific type
func FindProvidersByType(providers []catwalk.Provider, t catwalk.Type) []catwalk.Provider {
    var result []catwalk.Provider
    for _, p := range providers {
        if p.Type == t {
            result = append(result, p)
        }
    }
    return result
}

// FindModelsWithReasoning returns all models that support extended reasoning
func FindModelsWithReasoning(providers []catwalk.Provider) []struct {
    Provider *catwalk.Provider
    Model    *catwalk.Model
} {
    var results []struct {
        Provider *catwalk.Provider
        Model    *catwalk.Model
    }

    for i := range providers {
        for j := range providers[i].Models {
            if providers[i].Models[j].CanReason {
                results = append(results, struct {
                    Provider *catwalk.Provider
                    Model    *catwalk.Model
                }{
                    Provider: &providers[i],
                    Model:    &providers[i].Models[j],
                })
            }
        }
    }
    return results
}

func main() {
    providers := embedded.GetAll()

    // Find all OpenAI-compatible providers
    openaiCompat := FindProvidersByType(providers, catwalk.TypeOpenAICompat)
    log.Printf("Found %d OpenAI-compatible providers\n", len(openaiCompat))

    // Find all models with reasoning
    reasoningModels := FindModelsWithReasoning(providers)
    log.Printf("Found %d models with reasoning capability\n", len(reasoningModels))
    for _, rm := range reasoningModels {
        log.Printf("  %s - %s\n", rm.Provider.Name, rm.Model.Name)
    }
}
```

